[971.794808, "o", "[SEARCH] 搜索结果: 共找到 23 处匹配，分布在 2 个文件中\r\n================================================================================\r\n\\n[FILE] mdftypes.h (10 处匹配)\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    [上下文]\\n      19 | ///\\n      20 | //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\r\n>>>   21 | struct MdfHeader \r\n      22 | { \\n      23 | \tchar cId[8]; // 'MDF v1.0'\r\n    [上下文]\\n     189 | /// once the file is loaded they are converted into memory locations.\\n     190 | /// \\par\r\n>>>  191 | /// The TMdfMesh Object contains all the information needed to display a mesh\r\n     192 | /// In addition to vertex information, the Mesh Object stores optional\\n     193 | /// bind-pose matrix array for animation as well as parenting information\r\n    [上下文]\\n     195 | /// \\par\\n     196 | /// Both of the arrays are parallel to the joint-keyframe\r\n>>>  197 | /// arrays in the the TMdfAnimation Object that corresponds to this mesh.\r\n     198 | ///\\n     199 | ///\r\n"]
[971.795075, "o", "    [上下文]\\n     199 | ///\\n     200 | //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\r\n>>>  201 | struct TMdfMesh\r\n     202 | {\\n     203 | \tunsigned int\tnNumVerts;\t\t///< Number of vertices in this mesh\r\n    [上下文]\\n     250 | \\n     251 | \t///\r\n>>>  252 | \t/// Mesh Type used by TMdfMesh::meshType value\r\n     253 | \t///\\n     254 | \tenum MeshType {\r\n    [上下文]\\n     301 | /// \\remarks The timeline is the animation channel for a single joint.\\n     302 | /// Timelines store the collection of keyframes for a single joint.\r\n>>>  303 | /// An array of timelines is stored in the TMdfAnimation object. The array\r\n     304 | /// corresponds to the depth-first sequence of joints. This array is \\n     305 | /// parallel to the bind and parenting arrays in the corresponding TMdfMesh\r\n    [上下文]\\n     303 | /// An array of timelines is stored in the TMdfAnimation object. The array\\n     304 | /// corresponds to the depth-first sequence of joints. This array is \r\n>>>  305 | /// parallel to the bind and parenting arrays in the corresponding TMdfMesh\r\n     306 | /// object.\\n     307 | ///\r\n    [上下文]\\n     327 | /// \\remarks All joint keyframe transformations are relative to their\\n     328 | ///\t\t\t parent joints. The parent joint information can be obtained\r\n>>>  329 | ///\t\t\t from the TMdfMesh::uPrnt.pParentInfo array.\r\n     330 | ///\\n     331 | ///\t\\par\t The order at which the timelines are stored in the pTimeline\r\n    [上下文]\\n     330 | ///\\n     331 | ///\t\\par\t The order at which the timelines are stored in the pTimeline\r\n>>>  332 | ///\t\t\t array corresponds to the same order as in the TMdfMesh's\r\n"]
